== the rule, pure ==
the rule cuts at three samples, over four times the reference: true
a steady window five times the reference is cut once it has three samples: true
a window one and a half times the reference is never cut: true
a window exactly at four times the reference is not cut: the bound is strict: true
a dispersed window is not cut, however slow its minimum: true
... and the rule leaves it alone: true
one stall among clean samples moves neither the minimum nor the verdict: true
the gate keeps a minimum under it from cutting, and admits one at it: true
no finite positive reference, no cut: true
== one timing call ==
isolated: five times the reference is cut after three single launches: true
isolated: with no reference the same routine takes its whole window: true
isolated: one and a half times the reference takes exactly that whole window: true
queued, cc calibration: five times the reference is cut after three single launches: true
queued, cc calibration: with no reference the same routine takes its whole window: true
queued, cc calibration: one and a half times the reference takes exactly that whole window: true
queued, CUDA/HIP calibration: five times the reference is cut after three single launches: true
queued, CUDA/HIP calibration: with no reference the same routine takes its whole window: true
queued, CUDA/HIP calibration: one and a half times the reference takes exactly that whole window: true
fast queued: the singles under the batch target are all taken: true
fast queued: the timed window at its depth is cut after three batches: true
fast queued: ... each of them a batch deeper than one: true
== an executed cc search ==
rounds=0: every window ran in full or was cut after three samples: true
rounds=0: the report counts the cut windows: true
rounds=0: every floor and near window ran in full: true
rounds=0: every per-segment single ran in full, however slow: true
rounds=0: a single slower than four times the floor was timed: true
rounds=0: the search crowned at the floor, refusing nothing: true
rounds=0: a search with cut windows still commits its schedule entry: true
rounds=0: a whole-routine seed over four times the head was cut: true
rounds=0: ... and every whole-routine seed over four times the head was: true
rounds=1: every window ran in full or was cut after three samples: true
rounds=1: the report counts the cut windows: true
rounds=1: every floor and near window ran in full: true
rounds=1: every per-segment single ran in full, however slow: true
rounds=1: a single slower than four times the floor was timed: true
rounds=1: the search crowned at the floor, refusing nothing: true
rounds=1: a search with cut windows still commits its schedule entry: true
rounds=1: the first whole-routine seed timed is the hopeless one, and it ran in full: true
